🐍 Python Learning Journey
This folder captures my hands-on Python journey — from basics to small projects, scripts, and experiments.
I’m learning by building, iterating, and documenting key takeaways as I explore Python for ETL, automation, and problem-solving.

🎯 Purpose
Practice Python fundamentals and real-world coding
Build small utilities and mini-projects
Apply Python to data handling, APIs, and automation
Document my growth and lessons learned

📂 Structure
basics/ – Syntax, loops, functions, data types
scripts/ – Small utilities and experiments
mini_projects/ – Practical mini-projects
notes/ – Tips, snippets, and reflections

🔑 My Approach
Learn by building → no passive reading
Iterate constantly → refactor as I improve
Document everything → notes for myself and for others
Celebrate small wins and track progress
